      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Acute pelvic pains in women can reflect highly diverse disorders of varying severity, sometimes requiring surgery. It thus is clearly a part of abdominal emergencies in the adult. Good knowledge of underlying gynaecological disorders usually avoids unnecessary surgery. The use of echography has greatly contributed to reducing coelioscopy for diagnosis."},
